                <pb facs="0516" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/87: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-21T16:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>70. From Surgeon General Cumming to Surgeon H. F. Smith: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In answer to your telegram dated August 20, in which your recall was
                            suggested, it is advisable for you to continue on the present detail
                            until the financial reorganization has been completed in October. You
                            are, meanwhile, authorized in your discretion to visit at expense of the
                            service neighboring West African countries to observe the local
                            activities for the control of quarantinable diseases and to return not
                            later than the latter part of September to Monrovia.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
